exit=2

### 2. the generated file deleted
python3 scripts/generate-topology.py --check
site-data: REFUSED
site/data/topology.json does not exist. The page fetches it; a missing file is a blank map, not an empty one.
make: *** [Makefile:175: site-data-check] Error 1
exit=2

### 3. a count edited by hand in the committed file (the 2026-08-08 defect, planted)
python3 scripts/generate-topology.py --check
site-data: DRIFT
site/data/topology.json disagrees with infra/ and tests/.
Run `make site-data` and commit the result.
make: *** [Makefile:175: site-data-check] Error 1
exit=2

### 4. an assigned resource deleted from a module (stale assignment)
python3 scripts/generate-topology.py --check
site-data: REFUSED
stale assignment: infra/modules/observability :: aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.http_5xx is assigned but no longer declared
make: *** [Makefile:175: site-data-check] Error 1
exit=2

### 5. a node removed from a phase while its module is still instantiated (undrawn)
python3 scripts/generate-topology.py --check
site-data: REFUSED
undrawn: group cloudwatch owns resources in infra/envs/stage, which no phase node draws
make: *** [Makefile:175: site-data-check] Error 1
exit=2

### 6. restored
python3 scripts/generate-topology.py --check
site-data: clean - every resource assigned; 116 across 8 levels (55 permanent, 61 per cycle), 2 deliberately not shown
exit=0


## Added with the band and the cut (second patch, same session)

Test 7 below is kept BECAUSE IT PROVED THE WRONG THING. Deleting the OIDC
provider from infra/ turned the gate red - and red on `stale assignment`, which
fires earlier, so the `backed_by` check under test never ran at all. A break test
that goes red for a different reason is a green check wearing a red coat: the
control has to differ in exactly the one thing being tested. 7b is that control -
the citation is pointed at a resource that does not exist while infra/ is left
alone, and only the band check can speak.

